// TODO:
// This isn't necessarily the best example, as really it should probably involve some
// classes and such, but the point is...
//
// I think that the cycle checker needs to not consider these "deferred" reads of a
// variable as a read, as it really gets in the way of nicely using globals.
//
// Perhaps the simplest thing to do in the short term is say that a global (or class member)
// doesn't require further analysis if all it is is a single function definition.
//
// Another option would be to say that any references to globals inside function definitions
// in any initializer don't count, UNLESS that initializer calls the function directly or
//     a) makes a call to any function-typed variable
//     b) passes a function typed variable to another function
//
// So e.g. var hook1 = { fun whatever() { hook2(); } var irrelevant = some_other_fun; irrelevant(); }
//
// Would count as referring to hook2, at least in the short term, even though the ValCall could not
// possibly refer to whatever.

var hook1 = fun(cond: bool) {
    if cond { hook2(123); }
};

var hook2 = fun(val: int) {
    if val > 500 { hook1(false); }
};

fun init() {
    print("success"); //! success
}